# THE DEFECT, REPRODUCED ON A SECOND ARCHITECTURE.
#
# SDPLIB truss6.dat-s at DEFAULT SETTINGS, no environment variables, ~/benchkit/param_sdplib.sdpa.
# HOST: pi -- i9-13900K, 24 cores, x86-64, Ubuntu, gcc. The macOS/aarch64 reproduction is in
#       dd_race_truss6.tsv; this is the same defect on the other machine and the other ISA, so it
#       is not a toolchain artefact.
#
#   dd_race (v7.1.3-omp.2)   5 runs -> FOUR distinct objectives, all wrong:
#                            3.9521499916550376e+04, 3.6353612816197647e+03,
#                            3.9522422936534203e+04, 1.0821458315017234e+05,
#                            3.9521633104401415e+04
#   dd_cond (fixed)          5 runs -> -9.0100140477088098e+02 every time
#
# The correct objective is -9.0100140477088098e+02. Note that three of the five wrong values
# agree to four significant digits with each other -- a run-to-run spread test with a loose
# tolerance and a small sample could call that stable.
#
# arch0 rows are the control: two blocks, no shared entries, deterministic on BOTH builds. A file
# in which everything varied would not distinguish a race from a broken harness.
